.TH DANBY-PREDATORFISHING 1
.SH NAME
danby-predatorfishing \- predator and prey under fishing pressure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/predatorfishing
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Predatorfishing
adds equal per-capita fishing effort to both populations in a Volterra model.
.SH MODEL
X' = X(a-E-bY);
Y' = Y(cX-d-E).
.PP
X is prey, Y is predator, and E is fishing effort.  When a>E, the positive
equilibrium is ((d+E)/c,(a-E)/b).  Thus equal harvesting raises the equilibrium
prey population and lowers the equilibrium predator population: the classic
Volterra fishing effect.  When E is at least a, a positive coexistence
equilibrium no longer exists.
.SH DISPLAY
The phase portrait and time histories show the transient and shifted
equilibrium simultaneously.  The marked point is the analytic coexistence
equilibrium for the current controls.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to choose initial populations and the five bottom
tracks to change birth, predation, conversion, death, and fishing effort.
Space pauses, period advances one display step, r resets, and q or Escape exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The equation module is
.B /appl/danby/plugin/predatorfishing.b
and is regression-tested by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/predatorfishing.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/ecology.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-ecology (1),
